 ## 7. Discussion
 
-**What the two-level evaluation supports.** CARS-MODE attains higher proxy hypervolume than every external baseline tested, including NSGA-II with returned-population repair, GDE3, and NSDE. The FixedDE ablation is nominally higher and statistically unresolved, so the evidence does not attribute the gain to adaptation. The AC layer shows that selected plans can improve several network diagnostics while also demonstrating that proxy rank does not determine electrical rank. The 6.22% proxy advantage over the strongest implemented baseline followed by a mid-pack AC rank is the discrepancy that a proxy-only study would miss.
+**What the two-level evaluation supports.** CARS-MODE attains higher hypervolume than every external baseline under the archived sampled-bound, clipped indicator, including NSGA-II with returned-population repair, GDE3, and NSDE. That statement is configuration-specific: analytic feasible bounds and common-reference IGD+ do not preserve the CARS-MODE-versus-NSGA ranking in the compatibility rerun. The FixedDE ablation is nominally higher under every reported HV variant, so the evidence does not attribute a gain to adaptation. The illustrative AC layer shows that selected compositions can improve several network diagnostics while also demonstrating that the primary proxy rank does not determine electrical rank.
 
 **Why the adaptive controller remains exploratory.** FixedDE is nominally 0.60% higher at the proxy level, and the contrast remains unresolved in all seven planning experiments, so the primary evidence does not show a gain from jointly adapting parameters and strategies. The current control cannot determine whether one adaptive subcomponent helps while the other hurts. The AC inspection suggests a possible secondary role for the bundle: FixedDE selects one additional storage action in the base experiment (8 versus 7), and the mapped plan coincides with greater over-voltage in the rural network and less reinforcement in urban growth cases. This pattern is insufficient for a causal claim but motivates future electrically integrated search. More generally, proxy and external validation can assign different apparent value to a mechanism group; the corresponding contrast for budget repair (−6.84% proxy, AC-neutral in aggregate) reinforces the need to report both levels.
 
-**Why the complete framework can outperform controls without a resolved adaptation-bundle effect.** Removing diversity or repair reduces the effective set of feasible trade-off solutions, whereas jointly fixing the DE parameters and restricting mutation to rand/1 leaves that set almost unchanged. The direct GDE3 and NSDE comparisons show that the complete constrained-search pipeline is competitive relative to other multi-objective DE implementations, but the FixedDE result prevents attribution of that margin to either adaptive subcomponent. The framework-level and component-level conclusions are therefore distinct: the implemented combination performs well on the proxy benchmark, while repair and diversity—not adaptive control—are the mechanisms resolved by the ablations.
+**Why the primary framework result and component result remain distinct.** Removing diversity or repair reduces the effective set of feasible trade-off solutions under the primary indicator, whereas jointly fixing the DE parameters and restricting mutation to rand/1 leaves that set almost unchanged. The direct GDE3 and NSDE comparisons establish competitiveness only under the archived primary normalization. FixedDE remains above CARS-MODE under sampled and analytic HV, while NoDER becomes the strongest core method under analytic HV and empirical IGD+; neither variant supports adaptive-component attribution. The implemented combination therefore performs well under the primary proxy metric, but no normalization-robust framework or adaptation claim follows.
 
-**Practical reading for planners.** All runtimes are sub-second at the tested scale. Front-returning methods provide a trade-off set and dominate the scalarized controls on proxy hypervolume, but the AC composition check does not preserve that ordering; Standard DE has the highest mapped AC-feasible rate. CARS-MODE has its largest proxy margin under the tight budget (9.84%), yet its portfolios are not electrically dominant. The proxy front should therefore serve as a candidate-generation stage whose survivors undergo power-flow checks.
+**Practical reading for planners.** All archived runtimes are sub-second at the tested scale. Front-returning methods provide trade-off sets, but their ordering depends on objective normalization and is not preserved by the illustrative AC composition check; Standard DE has the highest mapped AC-feasible rate among covered methods. The proxy front should therefore serve as a candidate-generation stage whose survivors undergo preference-aware normalization review and power-flow checks.
 
